{"term":"barbecue","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:8a9bfcf8895d0681fd","definition":"A fireplace or pit for grilling food, typically used outdoors and traditionally employing hot charcoal as the heating medium.","example":"We cooked our food on the barbecue.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["braai","buccan","compare grill"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["banana cue","barbecue pork","barbecuer","barbecue sauce","barbecue slaw","barbecue stopper","barbecuey","barbie","BBQ","camote cue","ham barbecue","Korean barbecue","Lexington-style barbecue","Mongolian barbecue","nonbarbecue"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/barbecue#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:efcefe2e42a30880e9","definition":"A meal or event highlighted by food cooked in such an apparatus.","example":"We're having a barbecue on Saturday, and you're invited.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["braai","cookout"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["banana cue","barbecue pork","barbecuer","barbecue sauce","barbecue slaw","barbecue stopper","barbecuey","barbie","BBQ","camote cue","ham barbecue","Korean barbecue","Lexington-style barbecue","Mongolian barbecue","nonbarbecue"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/barbecue#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1565d7f05c9f7cb662","definition":"Meat, especially pork or beef, which has been cooked in such an apparatus (i.e. smoked over indirect heat from high-smoke fuels) and then chopped up or shredded.","example":"She ordered a plate of barbecue with a side of slaw.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["banana cue","barbecue pork","barbecuer","barbecue sauce","barbecue slaw","barbecue stopper","barbecuey","barbie","BBQ","camote cue","ham barbecue","Korean barbecue","Lexington-style barbecue","Mongolian barbecue","nonbarbecue"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/barbecue#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:770ae9350a6ea9b8b1","definition":"A hog, ox, or other large animal roasted or broiled whole for a feast.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"dated","register":"countable, dated, uncountable","wordFamily":["banana cue","barbecue pork","barbecuer","barbecue sauce","barbecue slaw","barbecue stopper","barbecuey","barbie","BBQ","camote cue","ham barbecue","Korean barbecue","Lexington-style barbecue","Mongolian barbecue","nonbarbecue"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/barbecue#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8c05055a19417863f7","definition":"A floor on which coffee beans are sun-dried.","example":"Drying the coffee beans took place in a barbecue, basically a large, flat platform, where the pulped coffee beans could be laid out and turned as they dried. Barbecues were often walled around and raised above ground level.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["banana cue","barbecue pork","barbecuer","barbecue sauce","barbecue slaw","barbecue stopper","barbecuey","barbie","BBQ","camote cue","ham barbecue","Korean barbecue","Lexington-style barbecue","Mongolian barbecue","nonbarbecue"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/barbecue#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:db50135942c7139551","definition":"A framework of sticks.","example":"1705, William Dampier, Voyages a